% n21: the impredicative existential, eliminated LARGE. `Ex : Sort 0 | mk : Pi (A : Sort 1). Ex`.
% Under max the constructor type is Sort 2 > Sort 0 and the inductive itself is refused (29).
% Under imax the codomain Sort 0 pulls `Pi (A : Sort 1). Ex` down to Sort 0, so the inductive
% is legitimately accepted -- that IS impredicativity -- and the only thing between it and
% `decode : Ex -> Sort 1, decode (mk A) = A` (a Sort 1 packed inside Sort 0) is the
% elimination restriction, 27. Two arms, two codes, one verdict: rejected.
1 sort 0
2 sort 1
3 const Ex
4 pi 2 3
inductive Ex : 1 | mk : 4
elim decode Ex 1
